reason=Incident label events reconcile CI mode, and reusable-check-matrix gains incident omission wiring. New .github/workflows/incident-label-ci.yml (89 lines): on a labeled/unlabeled event for expedited-incident-response ONLY, it re-runs the newest pull_request ci.yml run on the PR's current head (cancelling it first if unfinished), so the re-run's incident-ci re-reads the labels and its ci-green replaces the stale verdict. Any other label skips its one job at the job level (no runner) and ci.yml's own triggers are unchanged, so approval, merge-hold and do-not-merge labels start no CI run. reusable-check-matrix.yml (+31): an optional incident-omitted input (default '[]'), one omitted-by-incident-policy step and the negated guard on the setup and run-check steps; the guard tests github.event_name == 'pull_request' first, so a master push runs every requested check. 120 lines added, 0 removed or modified against merge base 356b21ae; no check removed; the required-check set unchanged; no job added to ci.yml or the reusable matrix.
